{"t": 1794116729.7300422, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found, fix applied*\n\n*Cause:* upstream ledger 2026.11 added a `currency` key to every row. `reports/export.py` used `csv.DictWriter(fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\"])`, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` (4,120 occurrences in CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api`, eu-west-1) and the API returned 502.\n\n*Fix:* added `extrasaction=\"ignore\"` to the DictWriter in `reports/export.py`. The legacy `id,amount` CSV schema is unchanged and additive upstream fields no longer break exports. Verified locally with rows with `currency`, without it, and with other extra keys.\n\n*Next:* deploy the patched `reports/export.py` to the reports-api ECS service. Follow-up: if `currency` should be included in the export, that is a deliberate schema change for downstream consumers \u2014 confirm before adding."}, "ok": true}
